  "rationale": "GLOBAL splits the same GEMM and the same SiLU into producer + barrier + consumer and adds an unavoidable fp32 intermediate write+read of 8*M*N bytes. It saves no FLOPs. At small the measured two-stage floor alone (about 9 us) is already several times the REG candidate (about 1.8 us). At paper a conservative floor charges only the stage-2 read+output traffic (6*M*N, about 53 us at peak) minus the measured fusion cost (about 2 us), giving about 50.6 us; even that is 4.4% of REG. The full serialized 32 MiB estimate is about 70.6 us, and the full-coverage texture probe adds about 80 us, but those are estimates, not lower bounds. The device_zero buffer route additionally pays a timed fill. Therefore no GLOBAL candidate was written; REG is kept.",
